course: dictionary
lesson: 9934
title: The tapir: a shy plant-eater
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: A tapir is a large animal that eats plants. Its body is a bit like a pig's, but it is not a pig. The clue is in its nose: «a short flexible snout» that works like a tiny trunk. When you meet a new animal name, look at the words around it to find out what it is like.
explain: «Tapirs are shy plant-eaters.» Shy means they are not bold, so they keep away from danger. The sentence gives a clue: «they hide in water from jaguars». A jaguar is a big hunter, so hiding helps the tapir stay safe.
explain: Test your guess against the facts. You might think a tapir is a pig, but the sentence says «their closest relatives are horses and rhinos, not pigs». When the facts do not match your guess, change your idea.
fact: A tapir is a large, plant-eating animal with a short, bendy snout like a tiny trunk.
fact: Tapirs live in forests in Central and South America and in South-East Asia.
fact: Tapirs are good swimmers and can slip into water to escape.
fact: Baby tapirs have stripes and spots for camouflage, and these fade as they grow.
fact: Tapirs are endangered because their forests are being cut down.
exercise: «Tapirs are shy plant-eaters with a short flexible snout that grabs leaves.» What does a tapir's snout do? | *Grabs leaves | Hunts jaguars | Breathes fire | Carries eggs
exercise: Ravi says tapirs are pigs. What do the facts say their closest relatives are? | Birds and bats | Jaguars and turtles | Pigs | *Horses and rhinos
exercise: Where do tapirs live? | Deserts in Australia | The open sea | *Forests of Central and South America | Ice mountains in the Arctic
test: Why are tapirs endangered? | They are too loud | They are too fast to catch | *Their forests are being cut down | They eat too many pigs
test: Why do baby tapirs have stripes and spots? | To look bigger | To attract birds | To swim faster | *For camouflage, to hide among the leaves
exam: Which sentence is true about tapirs? | Tapirs are fast flying birds | Tapirs live in the Arctic | Tapirs eat meat every day | *Tapirs are good swimmers
